  "behavior": [
    "Explicit manual binding selection is copied during construction. Empty selection disables provider acquisition.",
    "Selected declarations are checked before source work. Operation filters can only restrict the selection.",
    "Provider observations retain separate binding receipts through reconciliation and durable generation links.",
    "Provider calls share the configured concurrency limit. Queued calls observe cancellation.",
    "Strict mode requires exact source and binding observations. It accepts serving records without authored definitions and still refuses empty or degraded observations.",
    "Provenance preserves optional binding identity and revision through canonical JSON and YAML. Unscoped serialization omits those fields.",
    "Volume checks use history from the same binding revision and retain binding metadata when they classify degradation.",
    "Volume checks also require the same canonical provider ID. A reused binding identity cannot import history from another provider."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Manual CLI and HTTP adapters still need to pass shared binding settings and coordinate publication with runtime retention.",
    "History without a matching binding revision supplies no scoped completeness claim. Field provenance does not replace a complete scoped membership ledger.",
